<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>桌游 on 编程那些事儿</title><link>https://before80.github.io/prgms/tags/%E6%A1%8C%E6%B8%B8/</link><description>Recent content in 桌游 on 编程那些事儿</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>zh-cn</language><lastBuildDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:31:03 +0800</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://before80.github.io/prgms/tags/%E6%A1%8C%E6%B8%B8/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>桌游与扑克</title><link>https://before80.github.io/prgms/Language/English/Learn/dialogue/sports/board-games-and-cards/</link><pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 10:00:00 +0800</pubDate><guid>https://before80.github.io/prgms/Language/English/Learn/dialogue/sports/board-games-and-cards/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;桌游（&lt;code&gt;board games&lt;/code&gt;）在美国中产家庭和年轻人聚会里是&lt;strong&gt;主流社交活动&lt;/strong&gt;，比国内常见得多。一场 &lt;code&gt;game night&lt;/code&gt; 通常三四个小时，规则靠人讲、边玩边学，所以&lt;strong&gt;桌游场合的英语几乎全是&amp;quot;功能性对话&amp;quot;：问规则、确认动作、算分、辩解、认输&lt;/strong&gt;。&lt;/p&gt;</description></item></channel></rss>